ldren":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableFeatures"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tdata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../../index/type-aliases/RowData.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RowData"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../../index/interfaces/Table_Internal.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Table_Internal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../../index/interfaces/CellSelectionBounds.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CellSelectionBounds"}]},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const merges = table_getCellSelectionMergeBounds(table)","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"function-table-getcellselectionmergebounds","text":"Function: table_getCellSelectionMergeBounds()","level":1},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfeatures","text":"TFeatures","level":3},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"table","text":"table","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Function: table\\_getCellSelectionMergeBounds()\n\n```ts\nfunction table_getCellSelectionMergeBounds<TFeatures, TData>(table): CellSelectionBounds[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-selection/cellSelectionFeature.utils.ts:263](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-selection/cellSelectionFeature.utils.ts#L263)\n\nResolves the merged-cell rectangles of the rendered rows into selection's\nown index space.\n\nThe span index positions rows by their paginated render order while\nselection positions them by pre-paginated display order, so each merge is\nmapped through `row.getDisplayIndex()`. A merge whose rows do not map to a\ncontiguous display range is skipped defensively; it then behaves like\nunmerged cells instead of corrupting the geometry.\n\nReturns an empty array when `cellSpanningFeature` is not registered, which\nkeeps every selection code path identical to the span-unaware behavior.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFeatures\n\n`TFeatures` *extends* [`TableFeatures`](../../index/interfaces/TableFeatures.md)\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* [`RowData`](../../index/type-aliases/RowData.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### table\n\n[`Table_Internal`](../../index/interfaces/Table_Internal.md)\\<`TFeatures`, `TData`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n[`CellSelectionBounds`](../../index/interfaces/CellSelectionBounds.md)[]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst merges = table_getCellSelectionMergeBounds(table)\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: table_getCellSelectionMergeBounds\ntitle: table_getCellSelectionMergeBounds\n---\n\n# Function: table\\_getCellSelectionMergeBounds()\n\n```ts\nfunction table_getCellSelectionMergeBounds<TFeatures, TData>(table): CellSelectionBounds[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-selection/cellSelectionFeature.utils.ts:263](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-selection/cellSelectionFeature.utils.ts#L263)\n\nResolves the merged-cell rectangles of the rendered rows into selection's\nown index space.\n\nThe span index positions rows by their paginated render order while\nselection positions them by pre-paginated display order, so each merge is\nmapped through `row.getDisplayIndex()`. A merge whose rows do not map to a\ncontiguous display range is skipped defensively; it then behaves like\nunmerged cells instead of corrupting the geometry.\n\nReturns an empty array when `cellSpanningFeature` is not registered, which\nkeeps every selection code path identical to the span-unaware behavior.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFeatures\n\n`TFeatures` *extends* [`TableFeatures`](../../index/interfaces/TableFeatures.md)\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* [`RowData`](../../index/type-aliases/RowData.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### table\n\n[`Table_Internal`](../../index/interfaces/Table_Internal.md)\\<`TFeatures`, `TData`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n[`CellSelectionBounds`](../../index/interfaces/CellSelectionBounds.md)[]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst merges = table_getCellSelectionMergeBounds(table)\n```\n"}
